<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kerch</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Panticapaeum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kerch is a port city at the eastern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerch-strait">Kerch Strait</a>. It stands on the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panticapaeum">Panticapaeum</a>, a Greek colony founded by Miletus around 600 BCE that became the capital of the Bosporan Kingdom, and it later passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and, in 1774, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. It saw heavy fighting in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> and has been under Russian control since 2014.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kerch.jpg" alt="Kerch" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Solundir · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kerch_ObeliskOfGlory.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
